===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-|head=bona fide}}

# In [[good]] [[faith]]; sincere; without deception or ulterior motive.
#: {{syn|en|sincere}}
#: {{ant|en|mala fide}}
#: {{ux|en|Although he failed, the prime minister made a '''bona fide''' attempt to repair the nation's damaged economy.}}
#* {{RQ:Veblen Leisure Class|chapter=Devout Observances|passage=It is impossible to say how far this adherence to a creed is a '''bona fide''' reversion to a devout habit of mind, and how far it is to be classed as a case of protective mimicry assumed for the purpose of an outward assimilation to canons of reputability borrowed from foreign ideals.}}
# [[genuine|Genuine]]; not [[counterfeit]].
#: {{syn|en|authentic|genuine}}
#: {{ant|en|bogus|counterfeit}}
#: {{ux|en|This is a '''bona fide''' Roman coin.}}
#* {{RQ:Burroughs Mucker|passage=To Billy Byrne, then, Pesita was a real general, and Billy, himself, a '''bona fide''' captain.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|volume=47|issue=182|work={{w|The Christian Science Monitor}}|title=Ersatzes for Ersatzes|date=1955-06-30|url=https://archive.org/details/per_christian-science-monitor_1955-06-30_47_182/page/n17/mode/2up|passage=What intrigues us is what will happen when the ersatzes for the ersatzes come along. Will characters start substituting for actors, '''bona fide''' dogs for barking ladies; will people start looking at people again instead of television and at nature instead of at documentaries?}}
#* {{quote-av|en|year=2000|writers=Joel Coen; Ethan Coen|url=http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0190590/quotes|title={{w|O Brother, Where Art Thou?}}|passage= Ulysses Everett McGill: I am the only daddy you got! I’m the damn pater familias!<br/>Wharvey Gal: But you ain’t '''bona fide'''!}}

====Usage notes====
Sometimes misspelled as *''bonafied,'' by incorrectly analyzing as the past participle of assumed *''bonafy''.<ref>[http://www.wsu.edu/~brians/errors/bonafied.html Bonafied / Bona Fide], Paul Brians</ref>

